#####################################################
# Trivy ignore file for chisel/1-26.04              #
#####################################################

# Every entry below is golang.org/x/crypto v0.37.0, the version chisel v1.4.2
# pins in go.mod, and every one of them is in ssh/, ssh/agent/ or
# ssh/knownhosts/. Chisel imports only openpgp/{armor,clearsign,packet} and
# sha3 from that module, so none of this code is linked into /usr/bin/chisel.
# Trivy's gobinary scanner reports at module granularity rather than package,
# which is why they show up at all.
#
# Drop these once chisel bumps golang.org/x/crypto to v0.52.0 or later.
# References: https://ubuntu.com/security/<CVE-ID>

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/agent
# SSH client panic due to unexpected SSH_AGENT_SUCCESS
# Severity: High | Fixed in: 0.43.0
CVE-2025-47913

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh
# Unauthorized command execution via discarded SSH permissions
# Severity: High | Fixed in: 0.52.0
CVE-2026-39828

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh
# Denial of Service via crafted public key with excessive parameters
# Severity: High | Fixed in: 0.52.0
CVE-2026-39829

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh
# Denial of Service via resource leak from unsolicited SSH responses
# Severity: High | Fixed in: 0.52.0
CVE-2026-39830

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh
# Security key bypass due to missing user presence check
# Severity: High | Fixed in: 0.52.0
CVE-2026-39831

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/agent
# Security bypass due to improper handling of key restrictions
# Severity: High | Fixed in: 0.52.0
CVE-2026-39832

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh
# Denial of Service via crafted SSH certificate
# Severity: High | Fixed in: 0.52.0
CVE-2026-39835

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/knownhosts
# Revocation bypass via unchecked SignatureKey
# Severity: High | Fixed in: 0.52.0
CVE-2026-42508

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh
# Authorization bypass due to skipped source-address validation
# Severity: High | Fixed in: 0.52.0
CVE-2026-46595

# golang.org/x/crypto/ssh
# Denial of Service via crafted AES-GCM packet decoder inputs
# Severity: High | Fixed in: 0.52.0
CVE-2026-46597
